# Generation-read command alias: bounded unpaid diagnosis and proposed scope

Base: local reviewed `779eb26e706919780b9b5956b1337d0038678aaf`, integrated root equivalent `999b81e95351afb01184a941f6f150b165b8aeca`. Preparation only; no implementation authorization inferred. Completed correction, 680-entry evidence and performance limitation remain unchanged.

## Demonstrated failure

`StudioGenerationService.read` verifies and reads manifest bytes, JSON-parses and schema-parses them into a fresh local output, reads the admitted revision, then projects the selected proposal using `applyOperations(base.document, proposal.command.operations)`. The evaluator clones the base document but assigns `op.speech` and inserted items by reference. A later `set-text` mutates that speech, or later item operations mutate the inserted item. The returned proposal therefore contains altered operation payloads. The evaluator's final document schema parse produces a separate returned document; the retained command has already been altered by then.

The focused reproduction calls the actual read service with lower storage/source seams mocked, using the exact extracted original slot0 SSE arguments and the retained canonical final document. It passes final-document equality, unchanged manifest Buffer, unchanged shared revision row and repeat-read equality, then fails original-command deep equality. Original set-speech lengths 582/317/43 become 219/140/43 (the settle length remains 43 but whitespace changes). Operations hash changes from `351ad0cd6eea7b22f0423cc2cda48cd6436daefefd14e2dc1b961f4c4d6fcd7f` to `3f5a41e9a408d15f3dc08afdfa25452622b9cd56e47b94c74b825b9697d50422`.

`reproduction-isolation.log` additionally proves, without changing application code, that projecting cloned operations produces the same retained final document while preserving the original command. Returned document speech is not reference-identical to returned command speech after the evaluator's final schema parse. Both service calls repeat the defect from fresh parsed bytes; there is no accumulation across reads.

Invocation: `pnpm --filter @forge/admin exec vitest run .tmp/read-alias.test.ts --config .tmp/read-alias.config.ts`. One focused test intentionally fails on command equality; runtime about one second. Scratch harnesses are retained as `.body`. An initial mergeConfig merged include arrays and began unrelated unit tests; it was stopped, and the configuration changed to an exact single-file include. That setup mistake remains in `config-merge-failure.log`; it is not validation evidence for this scope. No production code, database, provider or historical fixture changes were made.

## Ownership and persistence assessment

- Persisted manifest object bytes are not written by this path: `readVerifiedStudioAsset` only resolves a ready version, reads bytes, and checks size/digest. JSON decoding creates new objects; mutating them cannot mutate the byte Buffer or underlying object storage.
- The revision row is parsed by `readRevision`, and `applyOperations` additionally clones the document. The reproduction deliberately returns the same row object on both reads and confirms no mutation.
- The selected request-local `output.proposals` entry is mutated and subsequently returned. There is no module-level parsed-output cache in this path. Read's transaction resolves source eligibility/subtitle bytes; it does not persist projected operations.
- No real-PG concurrency or storage roundtrip was run in preparation. Conclusions about persistent writes combine source inspection and a focused boundary reproduction, not a claim of newly executed DB proof.

## Callers and provenance impact

`apps/admin/src/services/studio-authoring/interactive.ts` dispatches `generation-read` to this method. Manager `generation-panel.tsx:130` loads it through `/api/studio/command` and trusted interactive transport. The panel uses `previews[0].document` for preview, displays `previews[0].proposal.command` as “Exact proposed operations”, and passes that command to `/api/studio/agent` for explicit Apply. Thus the displayed/re-submitted command can differ from the stored original and its operation digest, even when this saved case yields the same final composition. Do not generalize that same-result observation to every arbitrary operation sequence or intermediate validation.

Delegated RPC also admits `generation-read` under `studio:read` and reaches the same dispatcher. The current named Manager MCP tool catalog has no generation-read tool; native agent asset-tool catalog has no generation-read execution tool. They must not be described as direct callers merely because the delegated contract accepts the action. In-process tests also call the service directly. Hosted generation's completion stores the manifest before read projection; the read alias does not rewrite that stored output.

Original SSE arguments and original generation manifest remain original-command provenance. Closed `retained-0.body` preview command is already aliased final-state evidence and must remain honestly labeled. The canonical retained document remains authoritative for final speech; neither historical command nor document should be repaired in place.

## Smallest proposed implementation

In `generation.ts` read projection only, replace the operations argument with `structuredClone(proposal.command.operations)`. Keep the original proposal object for the response. Do not clone after projection (too late), clone individual speech fields (misses insert-item aliases), or change core ordered `applyOperations`. No response contract, prompt, schema/tool description bytes, hash algorithm, authority/source checks, persistence or provider behavior changes.

Tests-first at the actual service boundary:

1. Retained original SSE proposal: returned command deep-equals original parsed command; exact operations digest and whitespace preserved; returned document deep-equals historical canonical final document. Shared source bytes and revision object unchanged across repeated reads.
2. Minimal nested insert-item followed by set-text/set-properties/move/timing operations: inserted operation payload remains original while final document reflects ordered edits. Include opposite set-text/set-speech order to preserve existing semantics.
3. Two proposals and indexed reads retain correct selection and original commands; repeat reads do not alter other proposals. Existing project/revision binding, bad manifest digest, authority and source failures remain in force. Reuse existing canonical tests rather than widen interfaces.
4. Extend existing isolated PG generation retention scenario as needed to re-read registered manifest bytes and confirm no writes/changed revision during read; no paid calls or actual Apply is required to prove the clone boundary.

Run affected Admin tests/typecheck/build, focused Manager result parsing if needed, fixed-base Standards/Spec reviews and normal hooks after implementation authorization. No frontend code/chunk or tool schema change is proposed; the earlier mixed performance conclusion stays unchanged. No new performance or provider evaluation batch.

Await root scope decision before changing application code. All paid batches remain closed; creative/ElevenLabs acceptance remains incomplete.
